<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre d'Aubusson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1423">1423</a>–<a href="/years/1503">1503</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre d'Aubusson was Grand Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> from 1476 to 1503. He strengthened the walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodes">Rhodes</a> and led its defence against the Ottoman siege of 1480, in which the attackers were driven off. He later held the fugitive Ottoman prince Cem as a political hostage and was made a cardinal in 1489.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-daubusson.jpg" alt="Pierre d'Aubusson" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giovanni_barbagelata,_madonna_della_vittoria_con_pierre_d%27aubusson_e_i_ss._g.battista_e_pantaleone,_1503_ca.,_da_duomo_03.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
